<task id="131" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>C3 — the grant cache drops DirectAccessLevel, so a DIRECT grant on a secure root reads as None on every cache hit: carry the field, bump CacheVersion 4→5, and prove miss/hit parity through the real cache</title>
    <phase>Register-driven (authored 2026-09-30, session 27; verified defect C3 from session 26)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Authorization-path .cs change (the external grant cache feeds AccessibleRecordSetService's Secure suppression); tags bff-api/auth/testing.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security-boundary cache shape. The obvious one-line "fix" (default DirectAccessLevel to AccessLevel on read) is an OVER-GRANT on secure roots, and this exact bug class has already shipped twice (task 032 for AccessLevel, task 037 for DirectAccessLevel) with the suite green both times.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits ExternalParticipationService.cs, which task 132 (C12), task 109 (junction read), task 135 (CIAM veto pipeline) and task 137 (C5 revocation / grant-cache invalidation) also edit; Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/** is parallel-unsafe in this project. Tasks 132, 135 and 136 list this task as a dependency.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, security, caching, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Session 26 verified defect C3 (notes/session26-uac-defects-and-synopsis.md § C3), CONFIRMED by 3 adversarial skeptics; untracked (no task, no ISS entry, no GitHub issue). Owner round-2 decisions 2026-09-30 (notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md) — "no scope cuts, nothing deferred".</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>The external grant cache persists only (id, AccessLevel) per grant. DirectAccessLevel — the field Secure suppression reads — is dropped on write and comes back null on every cache hit, so a legitimate DIRECT grant on a secure project/matter/work assignment silently becomes AccessRights.None for most of every 60-second window. Carry the field through the cache, bump the cache version so no old-shape entry is ever read, and add the test that would have caught this: a real round trip through the production ITenantCache proving rights are identical on a miss and a hit.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer — external-access grant evaluation and its Redis data cache. You are fixing a cache SHAPE on the authorization boundary: an under-grant today, and an over-grant one careless default away.</role>

  <goal>For every grant the service returns, a cache HIT yields exactly the same ExternalGrantSet as the MISS that populated it — AccessLevel AND DirectAccessLevel, on projects, matters and work assignments — so AccessibleRecordSetService composes identical rights on miss and hit; CacheVersion is 5 so no v4 entry is ever served; and a shape-parity guard fails the build the next time a property is added to a grant type without being carried by the cache.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>🔴 THE DEFECT (verified against HEAD 2026-09-30 by this task's author; re-verify before editing).

The write projection, `CacheGrantSetAsync` (`src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalParticipationService.cs:1134-1168`), copies only `ProjectId`/`RecordId` + `AccessLevel` (`:1144`, `:1149`, `:1152`). The cached DTOs `CachedParticipation` (`:1242-1252`) and `CachedRootGrant` (`:1258-1268`) have NO `DirectAccessLevel` property, so `ToParticipation()` / `ToGrant()` leave it null. The miss path sets it (`:877`, `:896`, `:905`; org-inherited rows deliberately null at `:926`, `:933`, `:940`; dedupe carries both levels at `:959`, `:1009`). The hit path returns `cached.ToGrantSet()` (`:201-208`). `CacheVersion` is still 4 (`:39`) although task 037 changed the grant shape — contrary to the class's own rule at `:1281` ("CacheVersion MUST be bumped whenever this shape changes").

WHY IT MATTERS. `AccessibleRecordSetService.GrantedRightsFor` (`AccessibleRecordSetService.cs:237-259`) uses `isSecure(id) ? DirectAccessLevel : AccessLevel` (`:244`, `:250`, `:256`). On a HIT, DirectAccessLevel is null → `ExternalAccessLevels.ToAccessRights(null)` → `AccessRights.None` (`ExternalCallerContext.cs:207-213`). `AccumulateTerm` keeps the key (`AccessibleRecordSetService.cs:308-317`), so presence-gated reads still pass while rights-gated routes return 403 — to-do list/create/PATCH, document upload, event create (`ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs:399-401`, `:433-440`, `:570-582`, `:797-804`, `:897-909`). The cache is filled fire-and-forget (`:223`) and a workforce request runs three compositions in sequence (`CallerPrincipalResolver.cs:519-546`), so the answer can flip MID-REQUEST. Called from both workforce composers (`AccessibleRecordSetService.cs:1031`, `:1130`).

SCOPE OF IMPACT (from the skeptics): fails CLOSED (under-grant only); hits BOTH workforce planes — the contact-only plane (`ComposeForContactAsync`, grant term at `AccessibleRecordSetService.cs:1264`; session 26's own scenario is a contact-only Teams user on a secure matter) and the systemuser plane via the linked contact (`:1061`); the CIAM plane is unaffected TODAY because it reads only AccessLevel (`CallerPrincipalResolver.cs:378-429`) — but task 135 (CIAM plane onto the unified veto pipeline) makes the CIAM plane read DirectAccessLevel too, which is why 135 depends on this task; masked for a systemuser who also holds ADR-034 membership on the record; the cache is live whenever a `tid` claim is present and Redis is mandatory in deployed environments.

WHY NO TEST CAUGHT IT. Every existing consumer test substitutes `GetGrantSetAsync` wholesale — `UnifiedEvaluatorSeamTests.cs:892`, `StandingGrantRuntimeUnionSeamTests.cs:280`, `AccessibleRecordSetServiceTests.cs:1867`/`:1968`, `MembershipPagingCharacterizationTests.cs:673`, `ExternalAccessContractTests.cs:763` — so the cache is bypassed in every test in the repo. This is the THIRD time the pattern has bitten: the `:1273-1284` remarks record task 032 fixing the identical bug for AccessLevel ("correct on a miss, None on a hit … invisible to CI"). A fix without a round-trip test through the production cache would leave the door open for the fourth.

🔴 ORDERING WITH C2. Session 26 (§ Cross-links, § Consolidator notes): C2's presence-only read gates currently MASK this defect. When the C2 task (136, rights-based external read gates) makes reads rights-based, every C3 cache hit becomes a FULL denial (reads included). This task must land WITH or BEFORE 136 and 135; both already list it as a dependency.

DOC DRIFT IN THE SAME FACT. `docs/architecture/uac-access-control.md:67` still says the external participation cache is "version 3" (it is 4 today, 5 after this task). Correct it in this change so the version history in docs matches the constant.</background>
