  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003 / spec NFR-01">Scope: restoring a cached grant. A null DirectAccessLevel in the cache MUST restore as null — never defaulted to AccessLevel, never inferred. An org-inherited-only grant on a secure root MUST still compose to AccessRights.None (no key rights) on a hit, exactly as on a miss. Defaulting the missing field upward is an over-grant on every secure record reached only through an organization.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ExternalParticipationService.cs:1281">Scope: the cached shape. CacheVersion goes 4 → 5 in the SAME change that adds the field. It is the single public constant every invalidator references (`GrantExternalAccessEndpoint.cs:41`, `RevokeExternalAccessEndpoint.cs:36`, `ProjectClosureEndpoint.cs:41` alias it as `private const int CacheVersion = ExternalParticipationService.CacheVersion;`, and `SetRecordShareExpiryEndpoint.cs:345` uses it directly). Those aliases are references and stay as they are (task 137 owns consolidating the invalidation routine); do not introduce a literal version number anywhere.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 037 design (ExternalCallerContext.cs:75-90)">Scope: the model. Keep DirectAccessLevel as an additive field on the existing grant types. Do NOT change the dedupe to emit two entries per record id or collapse both levels into one — the remarks at `ExternalCallerContext.cs:83-88` explain why that yields list-order-dependent authorization.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 §7 (B1, B8)">Scope: tests. No Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; (B1) and no reflection into private members (B8). The miss path is reached by subclassing the PRODUCTION service and overriding a data-read seam — the convention every existing ExternalParticipationService double uses (`UnifiedEvaluatorSeamTests.cs:860-893`). If the grant query has no overridable seam, make the query method `internal virtual` (InternalsVisibleTo already covers the test assembly); do NOT override `GetGrantSetAsync` — that is precisely the method whose cache logic is under test. No DI-registration or ctor null-check tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="tests/CLAUDE.md TimeProvider rule">Scope: the round-trip test. No Thread.Sleep / Task.Delay / Stopwatch waits. The production cache write is fire-and-forget (`ExternalParticipationService.cs:223`). The test must be deterministic: assert the v5 entry exists (read it back through the same TenantCache) BEFORE the second call, so an unwritten entry fails loudly instead of silently re-running the miss. If that cannot be made deterministic without changing production behaviour, record the chosen approach and its rationale in the task notes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 KEEP paths">Scope: test location. The composition-level miss/hit test is a vertical-slice seam test → `tests/integration/seam/ExternalAccess/` (compiled into Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests via `Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests.csproj:149`). Use the PRODUCTION `TenantCache` over `MemoryDistributedCache` (construction pattern: `TenantCacheMetricsTests.cs:106-108`), not `InMemoryTenantCache` — the point is to exercise the production serializer.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR (BFF-touching). State the placement decision (in-place fix of an existing BFF cache; no new service, endpoint, package or DI registration). Measure publish size against a FRESH master worktree from a SHORT path, both sides zipped with Compress-Archive, file counts equal on both sides; report both absolute sizes and the delta; ≤60 MB. `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`: no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-30 (binding)">Scope: completeness. This task delivers a 100% fix of C3 — every root type (project, matter, work assignment), both levels, both the cache write and the cache read. Anything discovered during execution that is part of the same defect is added here, not deferred.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-10 (binding)">Scope: Dataverse verification. No Dataverse test in CI. Live verification is the MANUAL gate below, using existing non-admin test users in their current business unit — do not relocate users.</constraint>
  </constraints>

