  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor FULL. Re-verify every anchor in the background against HEAD — this project has recorded repeated premise rot; the code wins.</step>
    <step order="1">Add a nullable DirectAccessLevel to CachedParticipation and CachedRootGrant; write it in CacheGrantSetAsync and restore it in ToParticipation()/ToGrant() for projects, matters and work assignments, preserving null as null.</step>
    <step order="2">Bump CacheVersion 4 → 5 and extend the class remarks (`:29-38`, `:1270-1292`) with a v5 entry naming task 037's field and this task, so the version history stays complete. Confirm every invalidator still references the shared constant. Correct `docs/architecture/uac-access-control.md:67` ("version 3") to the current version.</step>
    <step order="3">Give the grant query an overridable seam if it has none (internal virtual), without changing its behaviour.</step>
    <step order="4">Write the seam tests per the closed set below: a production-service subclass that overrides only the query + flag/org reads, a real TenantCache over MemoryDistributedCache, an HttpContextAccessor carrying a `tid` claim, and the REAL AccessibleRecordSetService composition run once on a miss and once on a hit.</step>
    <step order="5">Add the shape-parity guard (criterion 7) and prove it bites by temporarily adding a dummy property to ExternalRootGrant (then revert).</step>
    <step order="6">Perturbation checks (criterion 9), each reverted before completion.</step>
    <step order="7">Build; full BFF unit suite; ArchTests; publish-size measurement per §10; CVE check.</step>
    <step order="8">Deploy to dev (bff-deploy skill) and run the MANUAL live gate (criterion 11); record the evidence in notes.</step>
    <step order="9">Record deviations and the determinism approach in projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-131-grant-cache-direct-level.md. Update TASK-INDEX.md status to `✅ [done]`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If restoring DirectAccessLevel on a hit changes ANY composed right beyond the C3 scenario (e.g. an org-only secure grant starts conferring rights, or a non-secure root's rights change), STOP — that is a second defect in the composition, not part of this fix. Report it with the reproducing test.</trigger>
    <trigger>If task 136 (C2 rights-based read gates) or task 135 (CIAM veto pipeline) has merged before this task — despite both listing it as a dependency — C3 hits are already FULL denials (136) or reach the CIAM plane (135) in any environment running that build. Report this to the owner immediately as a live regression, then CONTINUE: the fix is unchanged; only the deployment urgency changes.</trigger>
    <trigger>If no existing non-admin dev test user can exercise the live gate, STOP and ask the owner which user/record to use. "Can exercise" means: the user resolves to a contact (via sprk_primarycontact, or the verified-email fallback at `AccessibleRecordSetService.cs:1022-1027`), and a provisioned secure root exists that is NOT Restricted (Restricted vetoes all contact access — owner round 2 item 3) and on which the user holds no other membership. Do not create, relink or relocate users. Adding a DIRECT grant for that existing test contact on the dev secure test record through the product's own grant flow (and revoking it after the gate, both recorded in notes) is permitted test setup; editing any other grant is not.</trigger>
  </escalation>

