  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">1. POSITIVE (the C3 scenario): a contact holding a DIRECT Collaborate grant on a secure project composes Read|Create|Write on the cache MISS and identically on the subsequent cache HIT through the production TenantCache. The same assertion holds for a secure MATTER and a secure WORK ASSIGNMENT, and on BOTH workforce planes: the contact-only plane (ComposeForContactAsync) and the systemuser plane via a linked contact that holds no membership on the record (so the membership term cannot mask the result).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">2. NEGATIVE / authorization (no over-grant): a contact whose ONLY grant on a secure root is org-inherited composes AccessRights.None on the miss AND on the hit — DirectAccessLevel restores as null, not as AccessLevel.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">3. MIXED provenance: a ViewOnly DIRECT grant plus a Collaborate ORG grant on the same secure root composes Read only, on both miss and hit (the two levels survive the round trip independently).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">4. NON-SECURE root unchanged: an org-inherited Collaborate grant on a non-secure root composes Read|Create|Write on both miss and hit (AccessLevel path unaffected).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">5. NULL-LEVEL matter/WA row: a matter grant whose level is null keeps its id and composes None on both miss and hit (task 032's deliberate asymmetry preserved).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">6. VERSIONING: CacheVersion == 5; an entry seeded under the v4 key is NOT served by GetGrantSetAsync (the service re-queries), and every grant-cache invalidator in `Api/ExternalAccess/` obtains its version from `ExternalParticipationService.CacheVersion` — directly or through a `= ExternalParticipationService.CacheVersion` alias — with zero integer literals (grep evidence recorded in notes). `docs/architecture/uac-access-control.md:67` states the current version.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">7. SHAPE-PARITY GUARD: a test enumerates the PUBLIC init/settable properties of ExternalParticipation, ExternalRootGrant and ExternalGrantSet (the derived get-only views `Matters` / `WorkAssignments` excluded by name, with the reason in a comment), builds a grant set with a non-default value for each, round-trips it through the production write/read path, and asserts every property survives. Adding a property to any of the three types without carrying it through the cache fails this test (demonstrated once, then reverted). Any future exclusion must be named in the test with its reason (task 132's never-cached fault flag is the expected first one).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">8. The round-trip tests do not override GetGrantSetAsync, use no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, no reflection into private members, and no sleep/delay; the pre-hit assertion that the v5 entry exists is present.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">9. PERTURBATION: removing the DirectAccessLevel write (or the read) reddens criteria 1 and 7; restoring DirectAccessLevel as AccessLevel when null reddens criterion 2. Both reverted before completion.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">10. Build green; full BFF unit suite green; ArchTests green; publish size reported (fresh master vs branch, short path, Compress-Archive, equal file counts) and ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="false">11. MANUAL LIVE GATE (dev, after deploy): with an existing non-admin test user in its current BU whose linked contact holds a DIRECT Collaborate grant on a provisioned, non-Restricted secure root and no other membership on it (setup per the escalation trigger), repeat the Teams/SPA to-do list + to-do create on that record at least five times within one 60-second window, starting from a cold key (first call after deploy or after a grant write that invalidates it). Every call succeeds (no 403 insufficient_rights). NEGATIVE half: the same user on a secure root reached ONLY through an organization grant (if one exists in dev; otherwise state that none exists) gets 403 on to-do create on every call, miss and hit alike. Record user (by role, not name), record ids, timestamps, responses, and — where observable — evidence that later calls were cache hits (the v5 key present in Redis, or the HIT log line). Pre-fix baseline, if reproducible, recorded alongside.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">12. Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Defect C3 — `notes/session26-uac-defects-and-synopsis.md` § "[MEDIUM] C3"; owner decisions `notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md` (rounds 1 and 2 binding). Introduced by commit 392fc251b1 (task 037), already on origin/master.

